          "text": "## 2a43e4f3a796\n\n**Classification: reproduced API-contract defect; audit only, source unchanged.**\nAudited generator SHA-256:\n`6c977b7266d34103024a3670a6f7d2254c6e8e0b7b2060b0af1fe96f51496cc9`.\n\nThe focused reproducer `checks/audit/2a43e4f3a796/probe.py` calls the selected\ngenerator with five invalid argument combinations: boolean seed, float seed\n`1.75`, string seed `\"1\"`, boolean sample index, and sample index `-1`. All five\nwere accepted, produced grids, and returned no `self_check` errors. Exact inputs,\nshapes, observed schedule profiles, source hash, and limits are retained in\n`checks/audit/2a43e4f3a796/scalar_probe.json`.\n\nThe isolated audit-phase `defect_lint` independently failed. Its log records 24\n`strict-scalar` warnings across easy/default/hard probes, plus two broader\nself-check warnings. I classify the scalar acceptance as reproduced. I do not\nclaim the endpoint/minimal-shape warnings are label defects: the focused report\nexplicitly limits the finding to the call API and does not dispute that lawful\nendpoint grids may belong to the compaction domain.\n\nEvidence:\n\n- `checks/audit/2a43e4f3a796/scalar_probe.json`\n- `checks/audit/2a43e4f3a796/probe.py`\n- `checks/audit/2a43e4f3a796/defect-lint/result.json`\n- `checks/audit/2a43e4f3a796/defect-lint/checks/2a43e4f3a796_audit_defect_lint.log`\n\nRecommended repair: reject nonliteral integer seeds/sample indices and negative\nsample indices before constructing generator context, with portable regression\ntests. No target source was edited in this return.\n\n",
          "verification_status": "reviewer_reported"
        }
