          "text": "## 1d14de95c43e\n\n**Reproduced distribution shortcut; audit-only target left unchanged.**\nGenerator SHA-256 is\n`56ed271acad477a92d2ff734fd42e24a260fed37bba904d00c232fdbe9d9dd94`.\nThe documented rule chooses the most frequent nonzero colour per column, yet the\nproduction generator writes only one nonzero colour in each nonempty column.\n\nA deterministic survey of seeds 0\u201324, sample indices 0\u20133, and difficulties\n`None/easy/medium/hard` materialized **400 grids** and **2,800 columns**.  It\nfound **0 columns with more than one nonzero colour** and 239 empty columns.\nThus the rival \u201creturn the first/only nonzero colour in each column\u201d fits every\nnonempty generated column in the survey; frequency counting is never required.\n\nThe exact accepted input `[[4],[6],[6],[0]]` is a one-column counterexample in\nthe documented majority-rule domain.  The supported Racket authority (rule hash\n`2d8fe86a8d56`) returns `[[6]]`, while the first-nonzero rival returns `[[4]]`.\n`self_check` returns `[]`, but this multicolour-column case was not emitted in the\n400-grid production survey.\n\nEvidence and reproduction:\n\n- `checks/audit/1d14de95c43e/counterexample.json`\n- `checks/audit/1d14de95c43e/racket.json`\n- `checks/audit/1d14de95c43e/rival_output.json`\n- `checks/audits/reproduce_audits.py`\n- `checks/audits/reproduction.json`\n\nThe exact counterexample belongs to the validator/documented semantic domain,\nbut not to the measured production distribution.  Adding columns with a unique\nmajority plus at least one differently coloured noise cell would directly teach\nthe intended operation.\n",
          "verification_status": "reviewer_reported"
        }
      ],
